  "description": "<div><p>Evaluate an arithmetic expression s and return its integer value. The supported syntax is nonnegative decimal integers, binary + and -, unary - (including immediately before a parenthesized expression), parentheses, and spaces anywhere between tokens. Parentheses may nest. Consecutive minus signs such as 1--2 mean subtracting a negative value.</p><p>There is no multiplication or division: / is not supported, so integer-division rounding does not apply. The input is well-formed under the supported syntax; no implicit multiplication or unary + is used.</p><p><strong>Example 1</strong></p><pre>Input: s = \"1 + 2 - (3 - 4)\"\nOutput: 4</pre><p>Explanation: The parenthesized subtraction is -1, so 1 + 2 - (-1) is 4.</p><p><strong>Example 2</strong></p><pre>Input: s = \"-(8-(3+2))\"\nOutput: -3</pre><p>Explanation: The inner parentheses produce 5, then unary minus negates 8 - 5.</p><p><strong>Example 3</strong></p><pre>Input: s = \"1--2\"\nOutput: 3</pre><p>Explanation: The second minus negates 2 before the first minus subtracts it.</p><p><strong>Constraints</strong></p><ul><li>1 ≤ s.length ≤ 10,000.</li><li>Every integer literal is between 0 and 1,000,000,000.</li><li>The expression is valid and its final value fits in a signed 32-bit integer.</li><li>At most 100 pairs of parentheses are nested at once.</li></ul></div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def calculate(self, s: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the requested result.\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "var calculate = function(s) {\n    // your code here\n};\n"
  },
  "exampleTestCases": [
    {
      "inputs": [
        "\"1 + 2 - (3 - 4)\""
      ],
      "expectedOutput": "4",
      "explanation": "The parenthesized subtraction is -1, so 1 + 2 - (-1) is 4."
    },
    {
